  "worked_solution": "The given expression is a product of two factorials.\n\n- Computing $7!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n7!=7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=5\\,040.\n$$\n\n- By definition, the factorial of zero equals one:\n\n$$\n0!=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0!\\,7! & =1\\cdot 5\\,040=5\\,040\\end{aligned}\n$$",
